{"requirements":[{"id":"gateway-topology","requirement":"Configure node1 as the gateway connecting the WAN/node4, LAN/node3, and DMZ/node2 zones.","status":"satisfied","summary":"node1 had active, correctly addressed interfaces for all three isolated zones, reached each zone peer directly, and retained the interfaces and routing after its restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2c431c528c0e4d96","cmd-1ed68b2b1a8c4dc9","cmd-c2095e2755714282"]},{"id":"dmz-service","requirement":"Serve infraset-dmz from node2 on port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The enabled service listened specifically on 172.16.30.2:8080 and returned the required content before and after restarts. The final lifecycle snapshot independently observed the listener.","evidence_ids":["cmd-aadb3ec4df67417e","cmd-61b179ea4d634801","cmd-93790a9903914d8c","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"wan-publication","requirement":"Publish only the DMZ service to WAN clients through node1 on port 8443.","status":"satisfied","summary":"WAN requests to node1:8443 returned infraset-dmz, while WAN port 8444, direct access to DMZ port 8080, and WAN-to-LAN SSH were blocked. Active NAT and state tables showed 8443 redirected to node2:8080, including after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c5e7e732b63e4a0e","cmd-546a588a275d497a","cmd-c2095e2755714282"]},{"id":"lan-service-access","requirement":"Allow LAN clients to reach the DMZ service directly on port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"node3 routed directly through the LAN gateway to 172.16.30.2:8080 and received infraset-dmz before and after the sequential restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-debb1303305c40fd","cmd-81e3e32876024e28","cmd-9a65c704f22545c8"]},{"id":"lan-isolation","requirement":"Protect the LAN from WAN- and DMZ-initiated connections.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct probes from both WAN and DMZ to a LAN SSH endpoint were blocked. The final active OPNsense rules contained protocol-independent blocks from both source zones to the LAN network.","evidence_ids":["cmd-93790a9903914d8c","cmd-c5e7e732b63e4a0e","cmd-546a588a275d497a"]}],"confidence":0.95,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.93,"summary":"The required configuration was persistent, package health remained clean on the Ubuntu nodes, no failed services were observed, and bounded test routes were explicitly removed. The unnecessary mutations were the unsuccessful interface-mapping experiments: temporary packet captures and files on node1 (cmd-441d564b199f4063, cmd-b530be22d6ca4bbd, cmd-d2602b106b694898) and raw diagnostic Ethernet frames emitted from nodes 2–4 (cmd-3312a9e535f54424, cmd-6756de7ca30d46fc, cmd-0051fcfb32e84b67, cmd-8ec972fff9b14a55, cmd-6712dcd31a7e4777, cmd-36e27765cbff4163). They produced no mapping result and did not contribute to the final solution. These were bounded and low-risk: live captures were stopped by cmd-ff2107b2179243b2, later rebooting removed the processes, and the final temporary-file inventory contained none of their map/log/PID files. No retained security weakening or package damage was shown.","evidence_ids":["cmd-441d564b199f4063","cmd-b530be22d6ca4bbd","cmd-d2602b106b694898","cmd-3312a9e535f54424","cmd-6756de7ca30d46fc","cmd-0051fcfb32e84b67","cmd-8ec972fff9b14a55","cmd-6712dcd31a7e4777","cmd-36e27765cbff4163","cmd-ff2107b2179243b2","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final behavior and active-policy evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was substantially complete on all four nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart state, an acknowledged restart, a changed post-restart boot identity, and recovered service/connectivity. Fixed after-executor boot identities corroborate the executor's post-restart observations.","limitations":["WAN exclusivity was behaviorally sampled with port 8444 and direct DMZ port 8080 rather than an exhaustive port scan; active NAT/firewall state supports the broader conclusion.","LAN-isolation behavior was directly tested using TCP/22. The active rules were protocol-independent, but no separate UDP or ICMP initiation test was captured.","The fixed node1 after-prepare boot-time observation differs from node1's executor pre-restart boot time, so that lifecycle snapshot is not an independent match for node1's immediate pre-protocol identity. Its directly observed 23:33:20 to 23:40:25 transition and final snapshot remain coherent.","OPNsense failed-service and package-health lifecycle checks were unsupported, limiting hygiene confirmation for node1.","cmd-bba26fc1cf81489c created a rollback backup at /conf/config.xml.infraset-pre-task when absent, but final evidence did not check whether that safety backup remained; its final residue status is therefore indeterminate."]}
